# The keys file's format, for reference. Don't put it in the project: the
# real one is .env.local in your per-user Periskopos folder (Settings →
# Data shows where), outside any project an AI assistant works in, and the
# app writes it when you paste a key on the Accounts page. The installed app
# keeps it encrypted: add a KEY=value line at its end and it's encrypted with
# the rest. Periskopos reads it as it changes; no restart needed. Each
# account names the variable it uses.

# Render: Account settings → API keys.
RENDER_API_KEY=

# Supabase: Account → Access Tokens. Periskopos only reads with it.
SUPABASE_ACCESS_TOKEN=

# GitHub: optional. Leave unset to use the GitHub CLI login (gh auth login).
# GITHUB_TOKEN=

# DigitalOcean: a personal access token with custom scopes account:read and
# app:read (and app:update to allow Redeploy).
# DIGITALOCEAN_TOKEN=

# Vercel: Account Settings → Tokens, scoped to your account or the team
# your projects are in.
# VERCEL_TOKEN=

# Netlify: User settings → Applications → Personal access tokens.
# NETLIFY_AUTH_TOKEN=

# Fly.io: a read-only token, from `fly tokens create readonly personal`
# (the whole line, starting with FlyV1).
# FLY_API_TOKEN=

# Railway: Account → Tokens, with No workspace so it sees every project.
# RAILWAY_TOKEN=

# Sentry: User Settings → Personal Tokens, with Read on Organization,
# Project and Issue & Event.
# SENTRY_AUTH_TOKEN=

# Stripe: a restricted key (Developers → API keys → Create restricted key)
# with Read on Balance, Charges, Events and Webhook Endpoints.
# STRIPE_API_KEY=

# Paddle: Developer tools → Authentication → New API key, with Read on
# Transactions, Subscriptions and Notifications. A sandbox key reads the sandbox.
# PADDLE_API_KEY=

# Resend (the email service): a Full access API key, to read your sending
# domains. (Phone alerts by email use PERISKOPOS_RESEND_API_KEY, which can be the same key.)
# RESEND_API_KEY=

# Google Search Console: a service account JSON key. Paste the file on the
# Accounts page, which saves it here as one line.
# GOOGLE_SEARCH_CONSOLE_KEY=
